[#:seon.task{:name "each-commit-forces-the-directory-once-per-node"
             :kind :function
             :intent "FIXED ON THE KONSERVE FORK 08465d6 (reviewed; unpushed; adoption = push, apply tmp/commit-floor-research-opus/patches/adopt-konserve-deferred-sync.patch, restart; the store opts in with :defer-immutable-sync?; new immutable keys defer, existing keys and the head pay two directory full syncs): the JDK's FileChannel.force is F_FULLFSYNC on macOS (3.78 ms against 0.03 ms for FileDescriptor.sync); a settlement commit wrote 14.8 keys x 2 forces = 29.6 drive flushes, 71-76 ms of I/O; scratch replay: new keys 12-15 ms. Original: One small commit on default writes 4-8 index nodes (~120-175 KB each) concurrently and Konserve forces the store directory after each, then the commit record and the branch head each force blob and directory in order: 12-16 forces, device-serialized at ~4 ms each, ~45-50 ms of a 64 ms commit. The nodes share one directory, so one directory force after all node blobs are forced and renamed keeps durability and order (the record still lands after it): measured 38.4 -> 32 ms per commit shape (6 x 150 KB nodes + two ordered records). Needs a Konserve/Datahike fork change (write-pending-kvs!), not a config setting; the per-key path was ruled 2026-09-23, so bring it to the owner with this measurement."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.store/datahike-configuration}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/commit-floor-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/perf-eval-overhead-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/file-store-commits-pay-five-times-the-fsyncs-they-need.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-small-commit-rewrites-thirty-index-nodes"
             :kind :function
             :intent "At 128/32 (4d1f147a7) a 19-37 datom run on default writes 30-41 index nodes (180-260 KB, 235-336 KB on 4 KiB blocks) plus the 88 KB fused-root record, twice (commit record and branch head): 420-520 KB per commit, one commit per eval_clj run (2026-09-28 live attribution, tmp/store-writes/evidence.edn). AEVT and temporal AEVT are 55-65% of the nodes: every distinct attribute a commit touches is its own AEVT leaf, and the diff buffer does not absorb them. LZ4 store values (0241f02c9) halve bytes on the throwaway replay; remaining levers ranked in the evidence file: the head written as a second full record (each-commit-serializes-its-root-record-twice), the 4 KiB block floor (~25% of node disk; a packing backend trades it for compaction write amplification), temporal indexes (~40% of node bytes; keep-history is the as-of capability)."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.store/datahike-configuration}
             :evidence #{"tmp/store-writes/evidence.edn" "tmp/store-writes/lz4_proof.clj"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "index-roots-lose-their-subtree-counts"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Every boot logs datahike.query.estimate 'Index lacks precomputed subtree counts (old database format)': on default (created at 128/32) the EAVT, AEVT and all three temporal roots hold subtree count -1; AVET keeps 233,196. Not a creation flag, not keep-history, not our Datahike fork: persistent-sorted-set 0.4.137 Branch.java sets a parent's count to -1 whenever a mutated child's count is unknown, serializes the -1, and nothing recomputes it (a fresh store has counts on all six; 50 upserts on a throwaway store lost AVET's at diff-buf 0, tmp/store-writes/subtree_counts.clj). The planner then uses heuristic cardinalities. Counts cost one long per branch node (negligible bytes). A nuke restores them only until ordinary writes decay them again; the fix is in PSS: apply the add/remove delta (+1/-1) to a known parent count without requiring the child's count, then measure planner choices on default's slow queries."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.store/datahike-configuration}
             :evidence #{"tmp/store-writes/subtree_counts.clj" "tmp/store-writes/evidence.edn"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/growth/growth-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "each-commit-serializes-its-root-record-twice"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Datahike's commit! writes the same db-to-store value (the fused-root record, about 134 KB on default) twice, as the immutable commit record and as the mutable branch head, and konserve serializes each write separately: two sequential serializations on every commit's critical path (about 5-8 ms of the 26 ms of CPU a settlement commit spends outside I/O). One serialization written under both keys, or a head that names the durable commit record, removes one; either is a Datahike fork change."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.store/datahike-configuration}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/commit-floor-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-ordinary-commit-writes-26-files-and-136-kb"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Measured on live default (4b29a0689, 2026-09-28): a (+ 1 2) eval is one commit of 30 datoms over 19 distinct attributes and writes 23-28 files / 120-151 KB; a defn plus call writes 61-126 files / 394-801 KB (64 datoms over 44 attributes, about 6 KB per datom). One (+ 1 2) commit: commit record 21.7 KB and branch head 21.6 KB (16% each; :fuse-index-roots? inlines all six roots, written twice, writing.cljc:143-193/523-528), aevt nodes 63.7 KB in 15 files (47%), avet 17 KB (13%), eavt 11.5 KB (8%). The floor is O(distinct attributes touched x branching factor x slot bytes) plus two heads, not the datoms; the aevt/avet share follows from 19-44 one-datom attributes per eval. Done when the levers ranked in tmp/commit-floor/report.md section 4 are tried on a branch of the live store and a (+ 1 2) commit is timed and byte-counted before and after (unfused or single-written heads, fewer distinct attributes per eval settlement, aevt/avet node packing), with the store-writes tasks it builds on (a-small-commit-rewrites-thirty-index-nodes, each-commit-serializes-its-root-record-twice) closed or restated by the result. Also: per tmp/store-growth/report.md the store holds 346,605 files / 1.07 GB (98% index nodes, 43% of du bytes are 4 KB block rounding), collection has never run, and 412-426 dead branch heads (rehearsal 197, building-source 143, checkpoint 40) sit outside the roster."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.store/datahike-configuration}
             :evidence #{"tmp/commit-floor/report.md" "tmp/store-growth/report.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "collection-lists-the-store-keys-twice"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Konserve patches to drop the second k/keys listing in collection (astra-referenced-blobs), which lists 346k keys per pass. Done when collection lists once, timed on the live store size."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.store/datahike-configuration}
             :evidence #{"tmp/store-growth/report.md"}}]
